.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-chatgpt-review-package-20260908/PROMPT-CHATGPT-DEEP-RESEARCH.md:3:Deep-research task. Attached is a package documenting eight failed, pre-registered attempts to make an auxiliary "coordination/externality" Q-head (C3) improve energy efficiency in a multi-user LEO-satellite handover RL controller (`00-README.md`, `01-CHRONOLOGY.md`, the R7 and F1 results, the contracts, the physics code and the tape format). The two other heads (C1 per-user surplus, C2 action-set) are sealed; deployment is a masked argmax of Q1+Q2(+Q3/κ). The robust empirical pattern: the C3 targets are learnable and held-out-predictive, yet deploying the learned signal does not raise pooled EE (ratio of pooled bits to pooled energy) and often lowers it; a cheap kill screen with the full physical tape of every legal unilateral deviation also finds no EE support for two cost-shared/energy-share externality targets.
